Aerie-Purpose: Stop an extension from allowing cookies through chrome.contentSettings.cookies.set, which would let third-party cookies through although the user blocks them.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/extensions/api/content_settings/content_settings_api.cc (ContentSettingsContentSettingSetFunction::Run)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Patch 0006 locks chrome.privacy.websites.thirdPartyCookiesAllowed, but an extension with the
contentSettings permission could still set an ALLOW or SESSION_ONLY cookie exception. An
explicit exception wins over the third-party block (cookie_settings_base.cc,
kAllowByExplicitSetting), and a pattern such as *://*.com/* covers whole domains. The set
function now returns an error for every cookie setting other than "block", for any pattern
and either scope. Blocking cookies through the API, and reading, getting and clearing,
still work. Other content setting types are not changed.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/content_settings/content_settings_api.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/content_settings/content_settings_api.cc
@@ -234,6 +234,16 @@
           ->Get(content_type)
           ->IsSettingValid(setting));
 
+  // Aerie: an extension cannot allow cookies, because an allow (or a session
+  // only allow) for a pattern lets third-party cookies through although the
+  // user blocks them. Blocking cookies still works.
+  if (content_type == ContentSettingsType::COOKIES &&
+      setting != CONTENT_SETTING_BLOCK) {
+    return RespondNow(Error(
+        "Aerie blocks third-party cookies. An extension cannot allow cookies; "
+        "only the user can, in settings."));
+  }
+
   const content_settings::ContentSettingsInfo* info =
       content_settings::ContentSettingsRegistry::GetInstance()->Get(
           content_type);
